      "description": "Version reporting is NOT uniform, and the gaps are structural rather than oversights. Palworld reports its build on gameserver_info. Minecraft's version rides on its OTHER series (query B) because mc-monitor's relabeling blanks `version` on gameserver_up specifically -- that blanking is what keeps the Uptime% panel honest, so it is deliberate. Satisfactory appears nowhere here: its API reports no version at all. Query B filters on version!=\"\" rather than on a game label, keeping this a schema dashboard with no game= filter anywhere.",
